The implementation of the `org.apache.commons.compress.utils.IOUtils.skip` method is as follows:

```java
public static long skip(InputStream input, long numToSkip) throws IOException {
    long available = numToSkip;
    while (numToSkip > 0) {
        long skipped = input.skip(numToSkip);
        if (skipped == 0) {
            break;
        }
        numToSkip -= skipped;
    }

    return available - numToSkip;
}
```

The `IOUtils.skip` method uses a `while` loop to skip the specified number of bytes from the input stream. It breaks the loop if the number of skipped bytes is 0, which contradicts the behavior described in the javadoc.

